      "message": "fix(post): an absent rotary takes no angle word in fanuc and doosan-dnm\n\nThe RTCP arm block wrote A, B and C whatever the machine stated: on the\nA+B tilthead `G00 X0 Y0 Z20 A30 B0 C0`. Angle words now name only the\nrotaries in machine.rotaries; a turning letter of an absent rotary is\nstill refused by name (missingLetter runs first). doosan-dnm's RTCP\npath is the same code and gets the same fix; the other posts refuse\ntilted streams or write A only.\n\nPinned by the #926 recorded fanuc `rotary` golden (removed from\nKNOWN_BUGS), fanuc_post::an_absent_rotary_takes_no_angle_word and\ndoosan_dnm_post::doosan_dnm_absent_rotary_takes_no_angle_word.\n\nFixes #997\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
